cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this OneSTOP adaptation of wiSDM, please cite the archived
  software release and the upstream methodology article.
type: software
title: "wiSDM OneSTOP: Alien species risk modelling and mapping"
version: "2.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Gonçalves"
    given-names: "João"
    affiliation: "BIOPOLIS–CIBIO, University of Porto, Portugal"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OneSTOP-CIBIO/risk-modelling-and-mapping"
url: "https://github.com/OneSTOP-CIBIO/risk-modelling-and-mapping"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  OneSTOP Task 5.1 adaptation of the TrIAS wiSDM 2.0 workflow for modelling
  and mapping invasive alien species in Europe. The adaptation retains the
  core climate, habitat, and combined suitability modelling framework while
  adding user-supplied environmental inputs, custom spatial boundaries,
  integrated cross-validation, resilient multi-species chunk execution,
  monitoring and recovery tools, and strengthened raster and model handling.
  It is derived from TrIAS wiSDM v2.0.0, with upstream commit
  2c7bc8712304e46bebd1bbcf2f90771c4814f865 as the exact development base.
keywords:
  - invasive alien species
  - species distribution modelling
  - risk mapping
  - climate change
  - land cover
  - reproducible research
  - R
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Reproducible WiSDM: a workflow for reproducible invasive alien species
    risk maps under climate change scenarios using standardized open data
